<!-- wp:group {"className":"ifm-legal__body"} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ifm-legal__body"><!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"before","className":"ifm-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ifm-legal__h" id="before"><span>01</span> Before work starts</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Email <a href="mailto:support@iamfamous.uk">support@iamfamous.uk</a> with your order number at any time before we start and we refund the full amount. We normally start within one working day of receiving your details, so tell us quickly if you have changed your mind.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"after","className":"ifm-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ifm-legal__h" id="after"><span>02</span> After work has started</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you cancel after we have started, we work out the share of the plan that has been completed and refund the rest. We tell you how we worked it out. For example, if two of five pages of a website have been built, we refund the price of the other three.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Work that is finished and delivered is not refundable, except as set out below.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"monthly","className":"ifm-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ifm-legal__h" id="monthly"><span>03</span> Monthly plans</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A monthly plan covers 30 days of work. If you cancel part-way through, we refund the tasks not yet done. Monthly plans do not renew, so there is nothing to cancel at the end of the month.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"not-delivered","className":"ifm-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ifm-legal__h" id="not-delivered"><span>04</span> If we do not deliver what the plan lists</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Tell us what is missing or wrong. We put it right at no cost. If we cannot deliver something the plan lists, we refund that part of the price.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Links and listings that are not live when we deliver are replaced free. Guest posts removed within 90 days of publication are replaced.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"not-refundable","className":"ifm-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ifm-legal__h" id="not-refundable"><span>05</span> What we cannot refund</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We cannot refund money you paid to someone else, such as advertising spend, domain names, hosting or software licences. We also cannot refund a plan because a search engine, AI tool or social platform did not respond as hoped, since we do not promise results that depend on them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"consumers","className":"ifm-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ifm-legal__h" id="consumers"><span>06</span> Your legal rights</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you buy as a consumer, you have a legal right to cancel within 14 days of ordering. Because you ask us to begin within that period when you send your project details, you pay for the work done up to the time you cancel, and the right ends once the service has been fully carried out. Nothing in this policy reduces your rights under consumer law.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"how","className":"ifm-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ifm-legal__h" id="how"><span>07</span> How to ask for a refund</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Email <a href="mailto:support@iamfamous.uk">support@iamfamous.uk</a> with your order number and a sentence saying what you would like. We reply within one working day. Once a refund is agreed, we send it to the original payment method within 5 working days. Your bank may take a few more days to show it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
